this week on westworld  how much longer you've got to be alive  and it isn't long  multiple calebs a mole in our midst and  hail getting even more unhinged the  third last episode of westworld has come  to an end and i'm still pretty clueless  as to what's going on we're gonna get  going and stick around till the end of  the video where i go into my teaser  trailer spoiler section with hints on  where the show is headed we open on a  swing set whenever i think of sci-fi and  swing sets i always think of terminator  2. this is actually a flashback to  hale's takeover of the world via the  parasites frankie isn't that much older  in this scene than when she escaped host  carver in episode 3 suggesting that  hale's takeover was extremely quick this  is at odds with what she said in episode  4 that it took a generation for her to  gain complete control of the world so  maybe at this point she's only started  taking over california where this seems  to be set frankie and ewade have tracked  down a young jay who has started to  remember thoughts of his brother he'll  be picked up as an outlier before being  rescued this is the first place we've  seen other than new york in the 1920s  park that is equipped with these audio  transmitters at the safe house frankie  shows jay how she uses the radio and a  special frequency to send messages to  her dad but jay thinks this is a waste  of time her dad's gone just like his  brother this becomes an important scene  because it's here jay tells frankie not  to call him her brother later in the  episode when jay calls frankie his  family she knows he's a host because the  real jay would never call her that  frankie and bernard have arrived at the  abandoned 1920s park with the body of  maeve they found buried under the sand  two episodes ago if they're gonna get  her back up and running they'll need a  few things that can only be found here  in the background here you can make out  the madison avenue type area with  skyscrapers that we never really got to  explore and to the left a hidden easter  egg of the roman expansion a callback to  the original westworld film interrupting  a flashback of his daughter caleb wakes  up to find himself imprisoned under  hale's control she has this ominous red  hourglass which seems to indicate how  much time he has before his body decays  it's only a temporary body which will  break down in a matter of days of course  he wants to know where his daughter is  but hale reminds him he's not the only  one who has lost family a nod to her  family killed in season 3. hale has kept  kayla because she believes he is somehow  connected to her outlier problem a  problem which may or may not be related  to her host choosing to stay mortal  instead of transcend a process we saw  last episode hale also wants to know how  caleb disobeyed her order to kill maeve  those decades ago it was caleb after all  who told hale he has something she  doesn't we still don't know what this is  so hale thinks all these things are  connected hence why she keeps caleb  around hoping to get answers perhaps if  hale can capture frankie it will make  caleb talk and it's here we get our  first clue that within the rebels  there's a mole hale tells him that a  quote visitor is on their way we see  that caleb's build is number  278 the same number she told him in the  simulation from episode 4. caleb will  later find out his fellow prisoners are  earlier versions of him an apprehensive  frankie questions bernard about his  involvement with westworld and delos  she's still not sure what his grand plan  is they make their way underground in  search of a new control unit the one in  maeve's head would have been corrupted  after spending decades buried in the  sand ironically the control unit they  end up taking is that of temperance  hectors hector was maeve's love interest  in westworld and beyond it's also kind  of ironic that they awaken her in the  butterfly club the 1920s equivalent of  the mariposa where maeve spent most of  her life bernard says something really  interesting here that the original  founders of westworld started first with  a simulation and that hale has done the  same thing is this in any way connected  to what's happening with christina and  the quote-unquote game she's been  writing for the original parks were used  to collect data from their patrons  westworld used hats to do this but it  seems the 1920s world had improved tech  which utilized mirrors tech that played  off the most basic human impulse vanity  the processor found in the back of this  mirror will allow the data transfer from  maeve's old control unit into the new  one much more quickly back in new york  caleb is instructed by well caleb to  inspect the hourglass where he'll find a  device which pricks him and knocks him  out what he embarks on is a quest to  escape and get a message to his daughter  however this whole thing is a setup by  hail hale's been unsuccessful getting  anything out of him hell she's tried 278  times and failed so maybe by giving him  the illusion of hope she can keep tabs  on him and learn something that will  solve her problems when caleb is knocked  out he experiences memories of his  daughter and also those of his wife at  the hospital it's heavily implied he met  his wife here who is a nurse after the  incident at the lighthouse he awakens  with a drone host starting the  incineration process and escapes via a  conveniently placed grate with an etched  arrow pointing downward something that  was either planted there by hail or a  previous version of himself throughout  his escape he'll see several other of  his clones who didn't make it and i kept  thinking to myself how did hale not know  that there were all these dead bodies  everywhere but it doesn't really matter  considering this was all her plan anyway  bernard patches up maeve with that same  type of device that caleb used to treat  her gunshot wound in episode 3. we  learned that frankie's mom got sick and  it was frankie who took care of her in  her final days frankie is distrustful of  maeve considering she was the last  person she saw with her father the day  he left there's also a little talk about  how she believes hosts can't have  emotions and that their choices aren't  their own i wonder if this will change  over the course of the next two episodes  jay and stubbs arrive back with the  rescued outlier where jay tells the  group there's a mole this is how they  were discovered while in new york we'll  later find out this mole is j but jay's  human body was swapped with a host only  after they were discovered so is there  another mole or did the rebels just get  unlucky frankie initially shoots bernard  believing him to be the mold after she  discovered he was secretly copying her  he's trying to copy all of us all  bernard says in response to this is that  it's complicated and they need to trust  him jay wants to destroy me but frankie  refuses believing her to be the only  thing that has info about her father a  series of bloody handprints lead caleb  along this path of his previous clones  he'll end up finding a small room of his  exact same clothing even copies of his  wedding ring after a drone host almost  gets the better of him he coughs up  blood indicating that his time is short  because bernard has been through this  simulation thousands of times he knows  that the mole is one of frankie's  friends in fact the mole turned out to  be completely different people in  different simulations so he can't  pinpoint exactly who it is perhaps  bernard had frankie analyzed to verify  that she herself wasn't the mole  regardless he says that there wasn't a  single version of the simulation where  all of them make it out alive frankie  will either have to kill one of them or  they will kill her her paranoia has her  lock up her girlfriend odina the fallout  of which we'll likely see in the  episodes to come in one of the more  outrageous moments of the show caleb  uses a copy of himself to break his fall  from the ventilation shaft talk about  teamwork he has another flashback this  one of teaching an injured frankie that  the person who can't be beat is the  person that doesn't give up echoing his  own journey these past 23 years this is  a man who hasn't given up frankie  uncovers that it's jay who is the mole  he was switched while in new york he  tells her he doesn't want to kill her  and that may be because she's useful to  hail and can be used as a bargaining  chip against caleb speaking of caleb he  sends a message out to his daughter who  he refers to as cookie maybe that's why  she calls herself c he apologizes for  his failure as a father and not being  there for her he may have lost to hale  but she still has a chance it's a  message that she'll hear only a brief  portion of before jay shoots the radio  but it's maeve who saves frankie by  stabbing jay in the head for maeve it's  time for her and frankie to finish what  caleb started hale is frustrated caleb  spent all this time escaping only to  send what she calls a worthless message  caleb tells her it wasn't the humans who  infected the hosts rather that the host  would rather die than live in her world  this pisses her off and she kills him  we'll later see her picking at her scar  something we saw her do last episode  hale has all the caleb's incinerated it  kind of echoes what happened to james  delos senior in season 2 when it looked  like his quest for fidelity would not be  possible fidelity is the name of this  episode and refers to the process of  creating a human host hybrid to see if  they're true to the human they're  supposed to represent but hale isn't  giving up we see that the 279th  version of caleb is already being made  the marking of the great is covered up  perhaps hinting that hale has to try a  new approach we see her visiting this  new caleb in a rather interesting  position it's the same one he was in  while holding his gunshot wound in the  simulation suggesting this is hale going  through the same thing she did with the  previous versions he'll wake up run away  and be brought back in it seems the only  way she'll get anything out of caleb is  if she finally catches frankie but to  find out what happens we'll need to wait  for next episode up next is the teaser  trailer section where i go over some of  the shots we haven't seen yet to see if  there's anything we can learn i talked  about this one last week but this looks  like stubbs returning to new york or at  least some other populous city we'll  later see him at this abandoned  drugstore where clementine is there's  also this shot of what might be caleb  fighting clementine remember that  clementine was tasked with dealing with  caleb honestly if hale really wanted to  find frankie the best course of action  would be to let him go and track him  here's dolores or christina in some  water not exactly sure what's going on  here william shoots someone maybe it's  lawrence maybe not bernard is shot and  this looks far more serious than how he  was shot in this episode remember he  said there's no version of the story  where he survives a reflection of what  may be dolores christina with the  abernathy ranch william arrives at the  hoover dam where we see a big tear  similar to the one which led to the  sublime in season two william purchased  all the data in those servers there but  hasn't been able to get at them because  the files are encrypted i've theorized  that the real william may have switched  places with host william after host  william got infected so it may be the  real william who's chasing down hale at  the dam in this shot here's maeve  finally confronting charlotte looks like  she made it to new york and is that the  same knife that was used to kill jay i  also found this weird looking bell that  charlotte holds i wonder what that's for  this shot is super perplexing where we  can make out an early model of a host  exoskeleton we've seen dolores with this  in the past the man in black emerges  from the body-filled streets of what  might be california is this a flashback  to when the flies started taking over or  is this something else entirely maybe  he's hunting down the rebels so that's  pretty much it for this week i can't  believe we only have two more episodes  and the westworld saga comes to an end i  hope you'll consider liking and  subscribing as i'll be covering those as  well thanks for watching everyone and  for more bad takes you can follow me on  twitter and instagram at thinkstoryyt  until next time remember if there's  anyone who doesn't know what dallas is  well as we've always said dallas is the  vacation of the future today

